  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "The FY2025-26 recovery (organic +10% in Q3 FY2026, two guidance raises) is real but cyclical: restocking and data-centre/semiconductor capex carry FY2027-28, then discrete-manufacturing capex pauses as it has every 4-5 years, before reshoring and the software mix restore ~4-5% growth fading to 3%. Software & Control's margin gains (segment ~30%) are kept but not extended; Lifecycle Services stays flat-ish and Intelligent Devices remains a hardware cyclical. Capex runs above history through FY2029 on the $2B five-year US manufacturing and digital-infrastructure programme.",
    "bull": "Reshoring and tariff-driven factory investment turn into a multi-year North American automation cycle with no meaningful downturn inside the horizon; AI-enabled FactoryTalk/digital-twin software and recurring ARR lift Software & Control to ~30% of sales at low-30s margins, taking enterprise pre-SBC EBITDA to ~31%. Rockwell takes share from Siemens/Schneider in North American discrete and its installed-base switching costs convert the growth into durable aftermarket revenue.",
    "bear": "The current upswing proves to be restocking: as in FY2023-24, distributors destock and manufacturing PMI rolls over, revenue falls ~9% over FY2028-29 and margins give back the software-mix gains under negative operating leverage. Tariff and export-control volatility, China overcapacity and the larger diversified rivals' pricing keep recovery growth to 3-5% and the terminal margin at ~25.5%, below today's level, valued at a 13x cyclical exit."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Rockwell is valued as a quality cyclical on an owner-FCF basis: SBC (~1% of revenue) fully expensed, share count flat and funded by buybacks, mid-cycle rather than peak margins capitalised at a 13-19x exit. The market price capitalises roughly 33x trailing owner FCF, which the model can only reach if the bull case's decade without a downturn and structural margin step-up both happen; the gap between price and weighted value is the price of that thesis.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Cycle timing: a FY2027-28 destock (bear) versus continued recovery swings near-term FCF by 25-30%",
      "Software & Control margin durability: each 1pp of terminal EBITDA margin is worth roughly 4% of value",
      "Terminal multiple: the cap binds in the base case, so a market willing to pay 20x+ for automation exposure sits outside the house basis",
      "The $2B five-year US investment programme lifts capex above the 2.2-2.8% history; if it fails to earn a return, base FCF is overstated",
      "Tariff/IEEPA refunds and export controls on industrial control technology to China"
    ]
  },
